     1                                  ; LPTMOUSE.COM - DOS mouse driver (INT 33h) for a PS/2 mouse wired directly
     2                                  ; to a PC parallel port. See README.md for the cable.
     3                                  ;
     4                                  ; How it reads the mouse
     5                                  ; ----------------------
     6                                  ; The PS/2 clock is generated by the mouse (10-16.7 kHz). We cannot take an
     7                                  ; interrupt per clock edge, so the driver uses the host "inhibit" feature:
     8                                  ; holding CLK low makes the mouse abort and keep its data until CLK is
     9                                  ; released again.
    10                                  ;
    11                                  ;  IRQ mode (default, /I7 or /I5): CLK is released while idle. The mouse's
    12                                  ;  first clock edge raises the port IRQ (CLK is wired to /ACK). The handler
    13                                  ;  holds CLK low to abort that transmission, releases it, and reads the whole
    14                                  ;  packet in a tight loop with interrupts off (~3 ms). So the interrupt
    15                                  ;  latency does not matter, only the polling loop has to keep up with the
    16                                  ;  clock.
    17                                  ;
    18                                  ;  Poll mode (/I0): CLK is held low all the time. On every timer tick (18.2
    19                                  ;  Hz) the driver releases it for a few ms and reads whatever the mouse has.
    20                                  ;  No IRQ needed, but the cursor only updates 18 times a second.
    21                                  ;
    22                                  ; Build: nasm -f bin -o lptmouse.com lptmouse.asm
    23                                  
    24                                          cpu 8086
    25                                          org 100h
    26                                  
