    18                              <1>         ; byte(s) had already been sent: ask the mouse to resend the packet.
    19                              <1>         ; Nothing at all means the interrupt came after the whole packet
    20                              <1>         ; (something kept interrupts off for longer than a packet takes):
    21                              <1>         ; when interrupt driven, ask for it again too. The mouse only keeps
    22                              <1>         ; its last packet, so earlier ones missed the same way stay lost.
